"""Phase 3 sheet data: Accounts, Report, Service."""

ACCOUNTS = [
 ["9.1", "Invoice List",
  "invoice_list.php (list) > mng_invoice.php (direct, 1,672 lines) > quo_invoice.php (from a quotation, 1,447) > dc_invoice.php (from a challan, 1,457) > mng_credit.php (credit payment, 749) > inc/datatable/ajaxInvoiceList.php > invoice_print.php, quo_invoice_print.php",
  "TRANSACTION - THE STEP THAT REDUCES STOCK",
  "The invoice. One list, but THREE screens write into it depending on where the invoice came from, setting invoice_type so you can tell them apart. End of the sales chain and the only place stock comes down. A CREDIT invoice leaves a balance on inv_bal_value, paid off later through mng_credit.php. Cash invoices can record a denomination breakdown.",
  "tbl_invoice (RW)\ntbl_invoice_details (RW)\ntbl_invoice_pack_details (RW)\ntbl_invoice_denomination_details (RW)\ntbl_invoice_credit_details (W - one row per part-payment)\ntbl_item_stock (W - <branch>_stock REDUCED)\ntbl_stock_flow (W - trans_type 'INV')\ntbl_quotation / tbl_sales_order / tbl_dc (W - stamped as invoiced)\nmst_branch (R - the column name AND the print letterhead)\nmst_supplier_new, mst_customer_branch, mst_hsn (R)",
  "INSERT tbl_invoice (inv_slno, inv_finyr, inv_refno, inv_date, quo_id, so_id, dc_id, supp_id, branch_id, inv_tot_value, inv_bal_value, invoice_type, credit_amount, credit_due_date).\nDELETE + INSERT tbl_invoice_details, tbl_invoice_pack_details, tbl_invoice_denomination_details.\nPER LINE: read branch_stock_field from mst_branch; INSERT tbl_stock_flow (trans_type = 'INV'); RE-READ the current stock from the database; UPDATE tbl_item_stock SET <branch_stock_field> = current - invoiced.\nUPDATE tbl_quotation / tbl_sales_order / tbl_dc - stamped as invoiced.\nCREDIT PAYMENT (mng_credit.php): INSERT tbl_invoice_credit_details (inv_id, paid_amount, paid_date, mode, reference); UPDATE tbl_invoice SET inv_bal_value = inv_bal_value - paid.\nNO tbl_accounts ENTRY.",
  "1. Accounts > Invoice List - invoices for your branch with type, value and balance.\n2. THREE WAYS IN: Direct (Add New -> mng_invoice.php, invoice_type 'I'); from a quotation (Quotation List -> quo_invoice.php, type 'Q'); from a challan (DC List -> dc_invoice.php, type 'D').\n3. The reference is INV/0042/BIE/<branch>/<finyear>; the serial is MAX + 1 within your branch AND financial year.\n4. Enter or confirm lines, transport details, vehicle number, transport charge.\n5. Choose how it is paid. CASH allows a denomination breakdown. CREDIT sets a credit amount, due date and remark, leaving inv_bal_value outstanding.\n6. Save - header, lines, packing and denomination rows, then the per-line stock block.\n7. The source document is stamped so it cannot be invoiced twice.\n8. LATER, for a credit invoice: mng_credit.php records each part-payment and reduces inv_bal_value.",
  "Every stock figure in the system; Item Stock History via tbl_stock_flow; Credit List (invoices with inv_bal_value outstanding); Sales List and Invoice Report; the quotation, order or challan it came from; invoice_print.php on your branch's letterhead.",
  "THE STOCK DEDUCTION IS SOUND - like the GRN it re-reads the current quantity from the database before subtracting, so concurrent invoices both land.\nNOTHING STOPS AN INVOICE GOING NEGATIVE - there is no check that current stock is large enough, and the sales order reserved nothing and the challan moved nothing.\nTHREE SCREENS, ONE TABLE, AND THEY HAVE DRIFTED - mng_invoice, quo_invoice and dc_invoice are three copies of ~1,500 lines that do not do identical things. Change invoicing behaviour in all three.\nTHE INVOICE POSTS NOTHING TO tbl_accounts. No revenue entry, no receivable entry.\ninvoice_type: I direct, Q from a quotation, D from a delivery challan. A fourth value L exists on 13 old rows and is set by no live screen.\ntbl_invoice_credit_details has no reversal - a payment entered twice reduces inv_bal_value twice."],

 ["9.2", "Sales Receipt",
  "lst_sales_receipt.php (list) > pay_receipt.php (record, 693 lines) > inc/datatable/ajaxReceiptlist.php > inc/cis_ajax/jquery_modal_recipt_dets.php, inc/cis_ajax/modal_so_cash_details.php (view)",
  "Money in - AGAINST A SALES ORDER, NOT AN INVOICE",
  "Money received from a customer, recorded against THE SALES ORDER. Captures amount, date, mode (cash / cheque / card / transfer) with reference details, and WHICH LEDGER the money went into - the one place a customer's mst_ledger row is actually used. Advance payments work naturally: a receipt can precede any invoice.",
  "tbl_receipt (W)\ntbl_receipt_details (W)\ntbl_sales_order (R for the list; W to record the receipt)\nmst_ledger (R - the ledger dropdown, ledger_status = 1)\nmst_supplier_new (R)\nmst_finyear (R)",
  "INSERT tbl_receipt (so_id, supp_id, pay_slno, pay_finyr, ledger_id, pay_date, pay_type, pay_amount, pay_cardno, pay_refno, pay_chq_no, pay_chq_dt, pay_remarks, chq_passed).\nINSERT tbl_receipt_details - the breakdown rows.\nUPDATE tbl_sales_order - recording that a receipt exists.\nNO tbl_accounts ENTRY.",
  "1. Accounts > Sales Receipt - sales orders with what has been received against them.\n2. Choose an order; pay_receipt.php opens.\n3. Enter the date, the amount and the payment mode; cheque / card / transfer details appear as needed.\n4. Choose the LEDGER the money is going into.\n5. Save - receipt header and detail rows written, sales order updated.\n6. View receipts through the modals, or on the sales order print.",
  "Sales Order - the order shows what has been received; print_sales_order.php cash details; the receipt modals. NOT the Credit List, which reads tbl_invoice.inv_bal_value instead.",
  "RECEIPTS AND INVOICE BALANCES ARE TWO SEPARATE SYSTEMS THAT NEVER MEET. A receipt is recorded against the SALES ORDER and updates nothing on the invoice; an invoice's inv_bal_value comes down only through mng_credit.php. So money taken here does NOT clear an invoice from the Credit List, and a credit payment there does not appear on the order. USING BOTH SCREENS DOUBLE-COUNTS - pick one route per customer.\nNOTHING CHECKS THE AMOUNT AGAINST WHAT IS OWED, and there is no reversal.\nchq_passed is never set by anything.\nThe ledger dropdown lists EVERY active mst_ledger row, including auto-created customer, supplier and employee ledgers - and since nothing reads tbl_receipt.ledger_id afterwards, a wrong choice is never noticed."],

 ["9.3", "GRN Payment Details",
  "grn_payment_details.php (list) > grn_pay_receipt.php (record, 892 lines) > inc/datatable/ajaxGrnPaymentList.php > grn_payment_details_pending.php",
  "Money out - the supplier side, AGAINST A GRN",
  "The mirror of Sales Receipt on the buying side. Money paid to a supplier, recorded against a GRN - the goods receipt, not the purchase order and not the supplier's bill. The supplier's credit days set when payment is due. This and inv_bal_value are the WHOLE of BIE's money tracking.",
  "tbl_grn_pay_receipt (W - one row per payment)\ntbl_grn (R for the list; W to record the payment)\nmst_supplier_new (R - the supplier and their credit days)\nmst_finyear (R)",
  "INSERT tbl_grn_pay_receipt - the GRN, amount, date, mode, cheque and reference details.\nUPDATE tbl_grn - recording that a payment exists against it.\nNO tbl_accounts ENTRY.",
  "1. Accounts > GRN Payment Details - every GRN with its value, what has been paid and what is outstanding. grn_payment_details_pending.php narrows it to the unpaid ones.\n2. Choose a GRN; grn_pay_receipt.php opens.\n3. Enter the date, the amount and the payment mode with the cheque number or reference.\n4. Save - the payment row is written and the GRN updated.\n5. The list recalculates what is outstanding by summing payments against the GRN value.",
  "GRN List - the GRN shows what has been paid; this list and its pending version. NOT the supplier's ledger, which nothing updates.",
  "A PURCHASE RETURN DOES NOT REDUCE WHAT YOU OWE - purchase_return_add.php writes no accounting entry of any kind, so returned goods still show fully payable here. Check a GRN's returns before paying against it.\nPAYMENT IS TRACKED PER GRN, NOT PER SUPPLIER AND NOT PER BILL. No screen totals what is owed to one supplier, and the supplier's bill (supp_invoice_add.php) is a separate record this screen does not reconcile against."],
]

