SERVICE = [
 ["11.1", "Spare Mapping",
  "spare_mapping_list.php (list) > spare_mapping.php (map, 331 lines) > inc/datatable/ajaxMappingList.php",
  "Master - a link table between items",
  "Which spare parts belong to which product. One product, many spares - and both sides are ordinary rows in tbl_item_details, so a spare is just another item mapped to a parent. It exists so that a repair coming in for a product can be offered the right parts.",
  "tbl_spare_mapping (RW)\ntbl_item_details (R - BOTH sides, the product and the spares)",
  "DELETE FROM tbl_spare_mapping WHERE item_id = <this product> - EVERY row, before writing.\nINSERT tbl_spare_mapping - one row per chosen spare (item_id, spare_item_id, created_by, created_dtm).",
  "1. Service > Spare Mapping - products that have spares mapped, with how many each has.\n2. Choose a product, or add a new mapping; spare_mapping.php opens.\n3. Pick the spares that belong to it - all at once; this is a set, not a sequence.\n4. Save - every existing mapping for the product is deleted first, then the chosen spares inserted.\n5. The dustbin on the list removes a mapping through the shared delete endpoint.",
  "Repair Indent - the parts offered for a product being repaired. Nothing else.",
  "SAVING REBUILDS THE WHOLE MAPPING - open a product with forty spares, tick one more, and save a form that did not post the other forty, and you are left with one. Check the count after saving.\nTHERE IS NO STATUS COLUMN - tbl_spare_mapping has only the two ids and the audit pair, so unlike everywhere else in BIE, removing a mapping really removes it.\nNothing stops a circular mapping or an item being mapped as a spare of itself."],

 ["11.2", "Repair Indent",
  "repair_indent_list.php (list) > repair_indent_add.php (book, 961 lines) > inc/datatable/ajaxIndentList.php > sales_repair_print.php > inc/cis_ajax/jquery_sales_repair_status.php (verify and approve)",
  "Transaction with two-step approval - AND IT MOVES NO STOCK",
  "A repair booked in for something the customer already bought. Raised AGAINST THE INVOICE (inv_id), so the repair is tied to the actual sale and through it to the sales order and the quotation. Lines are the parts and labour, priced with tax. Then the same verify-then-approve pattern as a quotation.",
  "tbl_sales_repair (RW)\ntbl_sales_repair_details (RW)\ntbl_invoice (R - the invoice being repaired against; the stamp update is COMMENTED OUT)\ntbl_spare_mapping (R - the parts that fit)\ntbl_item_details (R)\nmst_supplier_new (R)\nmst_finyear (R)\ntbl_accounts - NOTHING (the posting code exists, commented out)",
  "INSERT tbl_sales_repair (sal_repair_finyr, sal_repair_slno, sal_repair_date, so_id, inv_id, supp_id, company_id, modify_by, modify_date_time).\nDELETE + INSERT tbl_sales_repair_details - the lines, rebuilt on every save.\nVERIFY (jquery_sales_repair_status.php, mode = verify): UPDATE sal_repair_verify_status, _verify_by, _verify_date_time.\nAPPROVE (mode = approve): UPDATE sal_repair_approve_status, _approve_by, _approve_date_time.\nNO tbl_item_stock UPDATE. NO tbl_stock_flow ROW. NO tbl_accounts ENTRY. NO tbl_invoice STAMP.",
  "1. Service > Repair Indent - repairs booked, with value and approval state.\n2. Add New; the serial is MAX(sal_repair_slno) + 1 for your branch, and the financial year comes from mst_finyear.\n3. Choose the INVOICE being repaired against - that brings the customer, the sales order and the quotation with it.\n4. Add the lines - spare parts and labour - with quantities, rates and tax.\n5. Save - header, then lines.\n6. VERIFY, then APPROVE, through jquery_sales_repair_status.php.\n7. Print with sales_repair_print.php. The quotation action on the list opens quotation.php, so a repair can be quoted for.",
  "Repair Indent List; sales_repair_print.php (the job sheet); Quotation - a repair can be quoted for. NOT the stock reports. NOT the invoice, which is not stamped.",
  "PARTS USED IN A REPAIR NEVER LEAVE STOCK - no stock table is touched and no tbl_stock_flow row written. With purchase returns (8.3) this is the second standing reason stock reads high.\nTHREE THINGS ARE WRITTEN AND THEN COMMENTED OUT: the tbl_accounts posting in jquery_sales_repair_status.php, the tbl_invoice.repair_submit_status stamp, and with it any way of telling from the invoice that a repair exists. The code reads as though the feature was built and switched off - it even looks up a sales ledger from mst_accounts_setting, a table BIE does not otherwise use.\nA REPAIR CAN BE BOOKED AGAINST AN INVOICE MORE THAN ONCE with no warning, because the invoice is never stamped.\ncompany_id on tbl_sales_repair really holds a BRANCH id - the serial is computed WHERE company_id = <your branch>."],
]

